title: 'pallet-collective: include the voting threshold in the proposal hash'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A proposal in `pallet_collective` is now identified by the hash of the SCALE encoding of
    `(call, threshold)` instead of the hash of the call alone. The same call proposed with
    different thresholds therefore results in distinct proposals. The derivation is exposed as
    `Pallet::<T, I>::proposal_hash(&call, threshold)`.

    The pallet's storage version is bumped to 5. Runtimes must add
    `pallet_collective::migrations::v5::MigrateToV5<Runtime, Instance>` to their migrations for
    every instance of the pallet. The migration re-keys every active proposal in `Proposals`,
    `ProposalOf`, `Voting` and `CostOf` under the new hash; an entry missing its call or its
    votes is logged and left under its old key. It is bounded by `MaxProposals` and runs in a
    single block.

    A proposal with `threshold < 2` executes immediately even while a motion for the same call
    with a different threshold is pending; before, it failed with `DuplicateProposal`.

    Breaking changes:
    - `Pallet::do_propose_execute` takes the `threshold` as its first argument.
    - Off-chain tooling that computed the proposal hash as `hash(call)` to call `vote`, `close`,
      `disapprove_proposal`, `kill` or `release_proposal_cost` must now compute
      `hash((call, threshold))`, with `threshold` encoded as a plain `u32` (not compact, as in
      the extrinsic), or read the hash from the `Proposed` event.
    - The `proposal_hash` in the `Executed` event, emitted when `propose` is called with
      `threshold < 2` and the call executes immediately, is also `hash((call, threshold))`.
      `MemberExecuted`, emitted by `execute`, still carries `hash(call)`.
    - Only active proposals are re-keyed. The deposit of a motion closed before the upgrade is
      still released with `release_proposal_cost(hash(call))`.
    - A call that names a motion by its old hash and has not run yet no longer finds that motion
      after the upgrade: a pending or scheduled `vote`, `close` or `kill` fails with
      `ProposalMissing`, while `disapprove_proposal` returns `Ok` and leaves the motion active.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The Alliance collective on Collectives Westend runs a one-off storage migration that re-keys
    its active motions. Motion hashes shown by tooling change accordingly.
crates:
- name: pallet-collective
  bump: major
- name: pallet-alliance
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-utility
  bump: none
- name: collectives-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: kitchensink-runtime
  bump: patch
